    fix for a mislabelled commit is a sentence in the next one, not a
    force-push on a shared `main`, and the cost is concrete: bisecting the
    timeout change lands on a commit labelled as a theme change.  Since then,
    staging has been checked per commit (`git status --porcelain` printed before
    each one, 18 / 13 / 4 / 3 files) precisely so this cannot recur silently.

