    two machines - 0.75, 1.04 and 4.2 - is the whole case for never asserting a
    duration.  Which is the whole
    argument for sizing the checks job's cap against the tail rather than the
    mean: 45 minutes is not a claim about how long this suite takes, it is a
    claim about how long a machine may be having a bad day before GitHub stops
    counting it as a result.  And the reason no cost gate in this package
    asserts a duration - every one of them asserts a count.
